From 81d40b1df4991b20d3d0ea26aced08f14a6f0dc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 04:19:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/25] test: cover the tmr() descriptor and P2MR wallet spends

descriptor_tests gains two tmr() vectors, a flat two leaf tree and a nested
three leaf tree whose Merkle root matches the internal tree of the tr() vector
above it, so the shared tree hashing is checked against a known value. Both go
through the full Check() path: parse, serialize, expand, sign and infer back.
The unparsable cases pin the single-leaf refusal and the tree syntax errors.

wallet_p2mr.py imports a tmr() descriptor, receives on the derived bcrt1z
address, spends it with send() and again through the PSBT flow, and repeats
both for a nested tree and for a ranged descriptor. It asserts the shape of
every P2MR witness (script path only, control block 1 + 32*m with m > 0 and
the last bit of c[0] set), that change is never P2MR, that the anyone-can-spend
single-leaf tree is refused, and that an active import warns about the missing
output type instead of generating P2MR addresses.
